WEBVTT

00:01:36.420 --> 00:01:38.790
Looks like we rattled the serpent's nest,

00:01:38.790 --> 00:01:41.340
and awakened a lot of trouble.

00:01:43.690 --> 00:01:45.660
1420.

00:01:45.660 --> 00:01:48.760
Our charged particle bombers failed.

00:01:54.500 --> 00:01:59.810
It used the electromagnetic energy to boost its shields.

00:02:03.380 --> 00:02:05.790
Fortunately, it's moving slowly.

00:02:06.120 --> 00:02:12.580
However, it'll still hit the Pilgrimage Point
in 180 hours at this rate.

00:02:20.230 --> 00:02:21.900
Type G-4.

00:02:21.900 --> 00:02:24.900
The EX-1 can't beat it,

00:02:24.900 --> 00:02:29.370
and none of our electronic weapons
have done any good.

00:02:29.370 --> 00:02:31.810
So how do we hold it back?

00:02:36.380 --> 00:02:38.280
Can anyone tell me?

00:03:33.800 --> 00:03:35.150
Mr. Fairy...

00:03:35.840 --> 00:03:36.810
Hattie.

00:03:38.710 --> 00:03:43.810
Sue, will those marks on
Mr. Fairy's hands ever go away?

00:03:43.810 --> 00:03:45.920
It'll be okay.

00:03:45.920 --> 00:03:46.900
...I think.

00:03:48.080 --> 00:03:49.520
You're not sure?

00:03:49.520 --> 00:03:52.990
The alien's surface armor
uses electric pulses...

00:03:52.990 --> 00:03:59.430
...to form liquid metal that fills
the cracks and repairs the damage.

00:03:59.430 --> 00:04:01.360
Suddenly, he's an expert.

00:04:01.360 --> 00:04:02.560
Whatcha want?

00:04:02.560 --> 00:04:03.230
Nothing really.

00:04:03.230 --> 00:04:04.460
It'll heal?

00:04:04.460 --> 00:04:08.390
It may take some time
for the scraped away parts.

00:04:08.600 --> 00:04:09.760
But it'll heal?

00:04:11.340 --> 00:04:12.310
Right?

00:04:17.580 --> 00:04:19.530
Y-Yeah.

00:04:21.380 --> 00:04:22.990
That's wonderful!

00:04:22.990 --> 00:04:25.290
Did you hear that, Mr. Fairy?

00:04:25.290 --> 00:04:27.490
You're going to be fine!

00:04:27.490 --> 00:04:29.010
Hooray! Hooray!

00:04:36.770 --> 00:04:37.830
Who was it...

00:04:37.830 --> 00:04:39.100
...that said it crashed...

00:04:39.100 --> 00:04:40.730
...and is making such a fuss?

00:04:41.940 --> 00:04:42.900
Here.

00:04:46.640 --> 00:04:47.570
Good.

00:04:51.780 --> 00:04:53.580
What are you staring at?

00:05:00.290 --> 00:05:01.950
What a weirdo.

00:05:19.140 --> 00:05:20.480
I guess we've lost.

00:05:20.480 --> 00:05:22.270
No, we haven't lost.

00:05:23.950 --> 00:05:26.070
We just haven't won.

00:05:33.220 --> 00:05:35.490
It's a tough opponent.

00:05:35.490 --> 00:05:38.690
It just freezes up into its shield.

00:05:39.600 --> 00:05:41.860
Like steel-plated armadillos.

00:05:53.910 --> 00:05:56.250
Thermonuclear is all that's left.

00:05:56.250 --> 00:05:59.180
Didn't you see how strong its armor was?

00:05:59.180 --> 00:06:01.680
We'd have to get close or it's a bust.

00:06:01.680 --> 00:06:03.520
But cruise missiles...

00:06:03.520 --> 00:06:04.650
We can do it.

00:06:04.650 --> 00:06:05.430
If we use that.

00:06:05.430 --> 00:06:06.400
You can't mean...

00:06:06.400 --> 00:06:08.060
I can.

00:06:08.060 --> 00:06:11.140
The EX-1 keeps it busy while we get close.

00:06:13.100 --> 00:06:14.400
It's possible.

00:06:14.400 --> 00:06:16.170
It's futile.

00:06:16.170 --> 00:06:18.730
It may have worked a few hours ago.

00:06:19.770 --> 00:06:23.110
But now that it's built up its armor...

00:06:23.110 --> 00:06:26.010
...it has EMP capabilities.

00:06:26.010 --> 00:06:27.010
So what-

00:06:27.010 --> 00:06:28.670
The signal won't reach.

00:06:30.780 --> 00:06:33.830
Even the SARGs can't withstand that EMP.

00:06:38.320 --> 00:06:39.790
So what do we do?

00:06:40.790 --> 00:06:42.730
Well...

00:06:42.730 --> 00:06:44.460
Shut up then!

00:06:44.460 --> 00:06:48.300
Getting all excited doesn't help.

00:06:48.300 --> 00:06:49.430
It's tea time.

00:06:49.430 --> 00:06:51.400
Though it's not really tea.

00:07:06.980 --> 00:07:09.420
You hate the coffee here that much?

00:07:09.420 --> 00:07:10.640
I'm sorry.

00:07:14.920 --> 00:07:16.670
I've got it, Lieutenant.

00:07:17.660 --> 00:07:19.890
I found a way we can beat it.

00:07:44.320 --> 00:07:45.360
Confirmed.

00:07:45.360 --> 00:07:47.790
Switching spray gun to manual.

00:07:47.790 --> 00:07:48.950
Sniping mode.

00:08:01.400 --> 00:08:02.370
Fire!

00:08:10.310 --> 00:08:11.520
Sampling complete.

00:08:14.950 --> 00:08:17.020
Right arm data complete.

00:08:17.020 --> 00:08:19.350
Let's get the leg next.

00:08:19.350 --> 00:08:20.320
Roger.

00:08:28.700 --> 00:08:30.470
Will this really work?

00:08:30.470 --> 00:08:31.900
Amazing, Lieutenant.

00:08:32.770 --> 00:08:36.410
All matter has molecular characteristics,

00:08:36.410 --> 00:08:38.580
and a unique signature.

00:08:38.580 --> 00:08:40.070
I've heard about that.

00:08:43.210 --> 00:08:47.850
So there's an inherent wave
projected to the outside world

00:08:47.850 --> 00:08:51.080
which can be amplified or reduced.

00:08:53.590 --> 00:08:55.890
This is fantastic!

00:08:55.890 --> 00:08:59.730
Agitating its shell causes
a molecular-level response.

00:08:59.730 --> 00:09:03.910
It triggers a defense mechanism
that increases molecular density.

00:09:04.230 --> 00:09:07.790
This alien can change its physical properties.

00:09:08.780 --> 00:09:10.170
Evolution!

00:09:10.170 --> 00:09:14.200
Yes, the metallic alloys respond
to the trauma by evolving.

00:09:16.750 --> 00:09:18.680
It's funny, Lt. Soma.

00:09:18.680 --> 00:09:21.050
It's like you're not your usual self.

00:09:21.050 --> 00:09:23.090
W-Well...

00:09:23.090 --> 00:09:26.320
You were a stratospheric test pilot, right?

00:09:28.090 --> 00:09:31.430
Did this love of science come from that or...

00:09:31.760 --> 00:09:33.360
SARG 5, can you hear me?

00:09:33.360 --> 00:09:34.360
Yes, sir.

00:09:34.360 --> 00:09:37.700
It wasn't easy getting that equipment.

00:09:43.470 --> 00:09:48.810
So will this really be
our holy sword, our Excalibur?

00:09:49.980 --> 00:09:51.850
It's like the story.

00:09:51.850 --> 00:09:55.180
Only the one destined to be king can use it.

00:09:56.220 --> 00:10:00.210
It looks more like some
torture device than Excalibur.

00:10:04.260 --> 00:10:06.630
The shield machine's in place.

00:10:06.630 --> 00:10:08.530
I'm returning to my office.

00:10:08.530 --> 00:10:10.930
We'll begin the reconstruction.

00:10:10.930 --> 00:10:11.900
Please do.

00:10:16.100 --> 00:10:19.210
I'd like a progress report
on SARG-5's objective.

00:10:19.210 --> 00:10:21.410
65% complete.

00:10:21.410 --> 00:10:25.150
We should have all the data
analyzed in 40 minutes.

00:10:25.150 --> 00:10:26.270
Understood.

00:10:30.020 --> 00:10:34.010
Now all that's left is for the hero
to take up the sword.

00:10:44.170 --> 00:10:45.470
Mr. Fairy?

00:10:45.470 --> 00:10:48.470
We'd like him to help us again.

00:10:48.470 --> 00:10:52.980
But his hands haven't healed yet.

00:10:52.980 --> 00:10:57.280
That's why we have a special tool for him.

00:10:57.280 --> 00:10:58.290
A tool?

00:10:58.290 --> 00:10:59.010
Yes.

00:10:59.010 --> 00:11:01.480
So he doesn't have to use his injured hands.

00:11:03.320 --> 00:11:18.370
Okay?

00:11:18.370 --> 00:11:21.470
Mr. Fairy says it's all right.

00:11:21.470 --> 00:11:23.460
Very good then.

00:11:48.130 --> 00:11:49.670
Will this really work?

00:11:49.670 --> 00:11:53.210
You don't like Lt. Soma's plan?

00:11:55.540 --> 00:11:58.970
We need innovative men to handle the aliens.

00:12:06.920 --> 00:12:08.810
SARG 5, come in.

00:12:08.810 --> 00:12:10.220
How's the analysis?

00:12:10.220 --> 00:12:11.490
All finished, sir.

00:12:11.490 --> 00:12:12.560
Now transferring.

00:12:12.560 --> 00:12:16.190
Figuring it out is quite a puzzle,

00:12:16.190 --> 00:12:20.320
but if we focus on structure,
we can find some answers.

00:12:22.060 --> 00:12:26.740
When it responds to outside trauma,
it absorbs sine waves.

00:12:26.740 --> 00:12:29.200
The system will keep absorbing vibrations,

00:12:29.670 --> 00:12:33.640
and thereby increase its amplitude to infinity.

00:12:33.640 --> 00:12:35.920
This will cause a structural breakdown.

00:12:38.850 --> 00:12:41.480
And I've used a non-linear equation

00:12:41.480 --> 00:12:46.020
to calculate the most vulnerable body part.

00:12:46.020 --> 00:12:47.150
That area...

00:12:49.090 --> 00:12:50.720
...is the left side of the chest.

00:12:51.790 --> 00:12:53.730
Get that, Mr. Fairy!

00:13:04.070 --> 00:13:05.370
Nice catch!

00:13:06.740 --> 00:13:07.800
Here we go.

00:13:09.140 --> 00:13:12.830
As long as the G-4 doesn't
have any tricks, we can beat it.

00:13:14.580 --> 00:13:16.320
Interesting...

00:13:16.320 --> 00:13:19.500
How are you always so calm
in the face of danger?

00:13:19.500 --> 00:13:21.510
You are, too.

00:13:21.510 --> 00:13:22.470
Me?

00:13:22.470 --> 00:13:23.730
Always.

00:13:23.730 --> 00:13:25.890
More so than Lt. Simmons.

00:13:27.930 --> 00:13:30.920
He used to be the cool guy of the outfit.

00:13:40.440 --> 00:13:43.780
You seem like you're ready to die anytime.

00:13:45.080 --> 00:13:47.210
I'm not ready to die.

00:13:49.890 --> 00:13:51.740
Not yet anyway.

00:13:54.390 --> 00:13:56.290
You remind me...

00:13:56.290 --> 00:13:57.950
...of myself.

00:14:00.130 --> 00:14:01.720
I'm not ready to die.

00:14:09.340 --> 00:14:12.940
Commence
"Operation Tuning Fork."

00:14:12.940 --> 00:14:15.580
Sue, monitor the distance.

00:14:15.580 --> 00:14:20.570
If you fall within its EMP area,
electrical devices won't work.

00:14:20.570 --> 00:14:24.150
But just what is
"Operation Tuning Fork," anyway?

00:14:24.150 --> 00:14:26.090
Ever do this in a science lab?

00:14:27.090 --> 00:14:28.890
Make sound waves.

00:14:28.890 --> 00:14:30.020
Hattie, ready?

00:14:37.170 --> 00:14:39.500
Excalibur vibrations nominal.

00:14:39.500 --> 00:14:41.040
Distance: 4000.

00:14:48.710 --> 00:14:49.480
Distance: 2000.

00:14:59.790 --> 00:15:01.980
EX-1 making contact!

00:15:14.740 --> 00:15:16.540
Exponential growth confirmed!

00:15:16.540 --> 00:15:17.500
It's working.

00:15:27.670 --> 00:15:29.520
Why didn't it stop him?

00:15:29.520 --> 00:15:31.190
It's altered structure!

00:15:31.190 --> 00:15:34.020
In order to shut out the vibrations...

00:15:34.020 --> 00:15:38.550
...the G-4 instantly altered
its outer shell's composition!

00:15:39.720 --> 00:15:41.930
It's like a sliding puzzle...

00:15:48.470 --> 00:15:49.400
Mr. Fairy!

00:15:53.940 --> 00:15:55.790
Where's his usual knockout punch?

00:15:55.790 --> 00:15:56.980
He can't use it!

00:15:56.980 --> 00:15:58.750
How do you know that?

00:15:58.750 --> 00:16:03.720
Because I've figured out where
the EX-1 gets his special power.

00:16:03.720 --> 00:16:09.020
He puts his strength in his left arm,
which was built from alien parts...

00:16:09.020 --> 00:16:12.130
...transforming the composition of that arm.

00:16:12.130 --> 00:16:16.730
He's been using it the way that
the G-4 uses its whole body!

00:16:16.730 --> 00:16:20.740
Like a magic arm, an alchemist arm.

00:16:20.740 --> 00:16:23.950
But neither the magic arm nor Excalibur...

00:16:23.950 --> 00:16:28.570
...will work as long as the G-4
alters its molecular structure!

00:16:38.090 --> 00:16:40.580
Then the solution is simple.

00:16:40.580 --> 00:16:42.080
I'm taking over!

00:16:47.330 --> 00:16:49.710
Mr. Fairy!

00:16:49.710 --> 00:16:50.380
Help him!

00:16:50.380 --> 00:16:52.330
No, we can't get closer.

00:16:54.270 --> 00:16:55.980
SARG 5's closing in!

00:16:55.980 --> 00:16:57.340
What?

00:16:57.340 --> 00:16:59.170
Into the EMP area?

00:17:07.320 --> 00:17:09.580
The FCS and ATC are both out!

00:17:09.580 --> 00:17:11.570
We have to turn back!

00:17:11.570 --> 00:17:12.790
Returning control.

00:17:12.790 --> 00:17:14.780
Keep it straight!

00:17:14.780 --> 00:17:16.190
What are we doing?

00:17:16.190 --> 00:17:18.590
You said it was like a sliding puzzle.

00:17:18.590 --> 00:17:23.050
So to figure the puzzle out,
we see what it looks like finished.

00:17:23.260 --> 00:17:24.300
It's useless!

00:17:24.300 --> 00:17:27.420
Our firing controls and sensors won't work!

00:17:27.420 --> 00:17:29.600
You're not ready to die, right?

00:17:29.600 --> 00:17:31.710
Then we won't die.

00:17:31.710 --> 00:17:33.560
Not you, not me.

00:17:33.560 --> 00:17:36.020
But in order to live,
we have to make this happen.

00:17:38.510 --> 00:17:39.650
All right.

00:17:39.650 --> 00:17:40.440
Let's do it.

00:17:40.440 --> 00:17:42.750
Good answer.

00:17:42.750 --> 00:17:43.790
Manual lock!

00:17:43.790 --> 00:17:45.720
Correcting for 5% error.

00:17:45.720 --> 00:17:47.060
Wind and human factors.

00:17:47.060 --> 00:17:49.090
You'll shoot with just intuition?

00:17:49.090 --> 00:17:51.180
That's why we had to get closer.

00:17:53.410 --> 00:17:54.080
It's futile.

00:18:04.240 --> 00:18:06.140
Fire!

00:18:06.140 --> 00:18:07.270
Analysis!

00:18:19.080 --> 00:18:20.030
That's not it!

00:18:20.030 --> 00:18:21.350
Next one.

00:18:25.860 --> 00:18:27.090
That's not it either.

00:18:31.400 --> 00:18:33.200
What about...

00:18:33.200 --> 00:18:34.870
No, still off.

00:18:34.870 --> 00:18:35.770
Next!

00:18:49.650 --> 00:18:50.430
That's it!

00:18:51.650 --> 00:18:53.140
Laser message from SARG 5.

00:18:53.140 --> 00:18:55.420
Aim at the left arm.

00:18:56.830 --> 00:18:57.950
The left arm?

00:19:00.460 --> 00:19:02.090
Mr. Fairy!

00:19:08.470 --> 00:19:09.900
Do it now!

00:19:09.900 --> 00:19:12.530
Before it transforms again...

00:20:26.180 --> 00:20:27.550
Mission accomplished.

00:20:27.550 --> 00:20:28.910
Returning to base.

00:20:51.260 --> 00:20:53.940
The electric parts have to be replaced.

00:20:53.940 --> 00:20:55.540
Couldn't be helped.

00:20:55.540 --> 00:20:56.880
Sorry about that.

00:20:56.880 --> 00:20:57.850
Forget it.

00:20:59.950 --> 00:21:02.750
Guess we weren't ready to die, after all.

00:21:06.320 --> 00:21:09.720
Thank you for helping Mr. Fairy.

00:21:14.300 --> 00:21:15.260
I...

00:21:17.030 --> 00:21:18.330
...helped him?

00:21:40.990 --> 00:21:42.090
That's wonderful!

00:21:42.090 --> 00:21:44.230
Did you hear that, Mr. Fairy?

00:21:44.230 --> 00:21:46.590
You're going to be fine!

00:21:46.590 --> 00:21:48.900
It's like you're not your usual self.

00:21:48.900 --> 00:21:49.790
Thank you.

00:21:49.790 --> 00:21:51.900
No! No!

00:21:51.900 --> 00:21:52.750
No!

00:22:28.200 --> 00:22:29.500
No...

00:22:30.110 --> 00:22:35.100
Sorrow and Malice

00:22:36.380 --> 00:22:38.810
Called by a name that isn't yours.

00:22:38.810 --> 00:22:41.780
A merry-go-round of hatred.

00:22:41.780 --> 00:22:44.780
You can't stop it or get off it.

00:22:46.420 --> 00:22:49.020
Next time,
Malice and Betrayal.
